\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath}
\title{Slice Timing Correction in Functional MRI}
\author{K. Osei}
\date{February 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Acquisition}
Functional scans sample each volume in an ascending interleaved order.
Roughly \frac{1}{2}$ of the slices are acquired before the repetition time midpoint,
which biases the estimated onset of the haemodynamic response in event related designs.
We correct the per slice timing offset before fitting the general linear model.
\end{document}

